test_edge_lengths -- cmo / addatt / edge_lengths_min, _max, _mean (Oct 2026)
=======================================================================

QUICK START

  sh run_edge_lengths_tests.sh [path-to-lagrit]     8 decks, about 1 s
  open summary.html

WHAT IS TESTED

  cmo / addatt / mo / edge_lengths_min  / att_name
  cmo / addatt / mo / edge_lengths_max  / att_name
  cmo / addatt / mo / edge_lengths_mean / att_name
  make a real (VDOUBLE) vertex attribute with the shortest, longest or
  mean length of the distinct edges at each vertex (cell sides; a tet's
  6 vertex pairs; quad diagonals are not edges); 0 for a vertex in no
  cell. The attribute name is required. Written to set a resolution
  from a surface mesh, e.g. the h field of createpts / poisson_disk
  from a DFN.

THE DECKS (meshes from make_edge_inputs.py, except el07)

  el01_equi    equilateral triangles of side 0.5: all values 0.5
  el02_rect    1 x 2 rectangles cut into triangles
  el03_quad    the same as quads (no diagonals)
  el04_mixed   quads and triangles together
  el05_jitter  a triangle grid with every vertex moved at random
  el06_lone    plus one vertex in no cell: 0
  el07_tet     a brick of cubes cut into 6 tets each (hextotet)
  el08_errors  no attribute name (none, or -def-): an error, nothing
               made; then a valid call works

WHAT IS CHECKED (check_edge_lengths.py)

  LaGriT finished; el_min, el_max and el_mean are real vertex
  attributes; every value agrees to 1e-10 (relative) with the value
  computed from the vertices and cells in the same dumped file; plus
  the deck's "# exact", "# lone" and "# refused" lines. On a LaGriT
  without these keywords every deck fails.

FILES

  run_edge_lengths_tests.sh   runner (work/, logs/)
  make_edge_inputs.py         the meshes
  check_edge_lengths.py       checks, summary.html (pictures with
                              ../test_lagrit_upstream/draw_meshes.py)
  el01-el08 *.lgi             the decks
